Good morning,

We are instructed to notify an escape of water on behalf of our client Beacon Mechanical Services, Inc. Our reference is FRC/GL/2025/8804.

The client's controller rang us this morning and was candid that she did not know which of their two placements this belongs on. We hold both their liability policy and their combined installation and equipment floater. Our view, and the engineer's, is that the primary file is liability with a companion floater file; the allocation schedule is attached.

Broker reference: FRC/GL/2025/8804
Insured name: Beacon Mechanical Services, Inc.
Insured trading as: Beacon HVAC & Plumbing
Date of loss: 7 February 2026
Loss location: 3400 South Cherry Creek Drive North, Denver, CO 80209
Cause: Escape of water - grooved coupling separation on a new riser
Estimated loss: USD 590,000

Our client's crew filled and pressurised a new chilled water riser on Saturday
afternoon and left site. A coupling let go at Level 4 in the evening and ran for
about eleven and a half hours before it was found on Sunday morning.

The building is occupied and operating. Three tenant practices are affected and
all three are closed - a dental practice has lost a wall-mounted panoramic X-ray
unit. The general contractor has already served an indemnity demand.

The building owner is a scheduled additional insured on our client's liability
policy for this project. Our client is not disputing that it was their joint.
The failed coupling, gasket and bolts have been retained and not discarded.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * mechanical failure investigation report
  * loss allocation schedule

Please confirm a claim reference on the liability file and a companion reference
on the floater. We are chasing the fill and pressure test record.

